ProteinBERT is a large protein language model trained using self-supervised learning on 106 million protein sequences from the UniProtKB/UniRef90 database [40]. It is capable of handling long-range dependencies within protein sequences. The embedding vectors produced by ProteinBERT not only capture the contextual properties of the amino acid sequence but also encode each residue’s physicochemical properties and potential interactions with distant residues [40]. We used the ProteinBERT pretrained embeddings in the form of a two-dimensional matrix of size [\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
